    "message": "Quantify full-output GBS errors and pure-core resources\n\nRun both routes on a common lossy 1152-output model. Establish full-click and actual integer-PNR error lower bounds, pair Frugal timings with scoped numerical accuracy, and repair tested B32 weight failures.\n\nBound pure-core energy and coherent truncation resources using fixed-basis native optimization and a known all-basis SDP. Retain numerical infeasibility, failed timing panels and representation limits. Full hardware throughput and full-distribution superiority remain unproved.\n\nValidation: 2502 independent checks; 982 tests run, 953 passed, zero failures/errors; fourteen new tests.",
